{"ranking": ["M1", "M4", "M2"], "fault": "M1 (NMOS common-source driver) is oversized, likely by roughly an order of magnitude (W=26.7 um where a value near 2-3 um is expected). At Vin=0.75 V it sinks far more current than the PMOS load can supply (about 40 uA from the M2/M3/M4 mirror), so vout_dc collapses to ~0.02 V and M1 sits in triode. That low output conductance explains the low gain (-13.8 dB) and low GBW (104 MHz)."}
